# Project Structure

Canonical layout for `frontend/`.

## Root structure

```txt
frontend/
├── .cursor/            # rules only, not imported
├── dev-plan/           # planning only, not imported
├── analysis_options.yaml
├── l10n.yaml
├── pubspec.yaml
├── assets/             # icons, images, illustrations, logos
├── env/
├── lib/
├── test/
├── integration_test/
└── tool/
```

## `lib/` structure

```txt
lib/
├── main.dart
├── bootstrap.dart
├── app/          # app.dart, locale, router, startup, theme
├── core/         # config, errors, logging, network, permissions,
│                 # responsive, security, storage, sync, utils
├── features/<feature_name>/  # data, domain, presentation
├── l10n/
└── shared/       # components, data, forms, layout, search, widgets
```

## Rules

- `features/<feature_name>` must own product behavior and screens.
- `core` must hold only cross-cutting infrastructure used by multiple features.
- `shared` must hold reusable UI, layouts, forms, and search helpers not tied to one feature; it is the only home for cross-feature reusable UI.
- Features must not fork parallel component libraries; check the shared catalog first.
- Must not place feature-specific business logic in `core` or `shared`.
- All user-facing text must be localized via ARB keys; no hard-coded strings in `lib/`.
- Must not create duplicate folders/files for the same responsibility.
- Tests must mirror source structure.

